<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto Tief</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a>–<a href="/years/1976">1976</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto Tief was an Estonian lawyer and politician who fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonian-war-of-independence">Estonian War of Independence</a>. In September 1944, as German forces withdrew, he formed a government in Tallinn on 18 September in an attempt to restore Estonian independence before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> arrived. The government was dispersed within days; Tief was arrested by the Soviet authorities and spent years in labour camps.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-tief.jpg" alt="Otto Tief" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otto_Tief.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
